    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "<thought\n>But resting feels like it's not enough. The fog is too thick to see anything else, and the weight is just... it's crushing. It's not even about being tired anymore. It's like the path ended because there's nowhere left to go that isn't just more of the same emptiness. It feels like the cliff isn't a mistake, it's just where the story is supposed to end.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
